QUICK REFERENCE: WEEK 1 COMMANDS
--------------------------------
Docker
  docker run -d --name X -p H:C IMAGE    run in background, publish port
  docker ps / ps -a                      list containers
  docker logs -f X                       follow logs
  docker exec -it X bash                 shell inside
  docker build -t name:tag .             build image
  docker push user/name:tag              push to registry
  docker network create / volume create

Kubernetes
  kind create/delete cluster --name lab
  k get nodes / pods -A / events
  k describe pod X
  k logs X
  k exec -it X -- bash
  k port-forward pod/X 8080:80
  k get pod X -o yaml / -o wide


TROUBLESHOOTING ORDER (USE IT FROM NOW ON)
------------------------------------------
  1. k get pods            -> what is the status?
  2. k describe pod X      -> read Events at the bottom
  3. k logs X              -> what did the app say?
  4. k logs X --previous   -> logs of the crashed container
  5. k get events          -> anything else happening?


